    },
    "Circle" : {
      "comment" : "Canvas shape type"
    },
    "Circles, snowflakes, rays, organic blobs. Four families, and you decide which of them the canvas is allowed to use — in Settings, under Appearance.\n\nThey used to be assigned: one family per category, whether you liked it or not. Now nothing is assigned. Every happening takes a shape from the ones you left on, a color from the day, and a place it keeps until midnight.\n\nNo metaphors. Just things that felt true." : {
      "comment" : "Note body: about_shapes"
    },
    "Clear" : {

    },
    "Close" : {
      "comment" : "DayCanvasViewer – close VoiceOver\nFull calendar – close\nMetricOverlay – close button\nPalette close button\nPayGate – close button VoiceOver label\nQuickStatus – dismiss button\nSettings sheet close button"
    },
    "Close quick status" : {
      "comment" : "QuickStatus – close VoiceOver label"
    },
    "Closes the quick status view" : {
      "comment" : "QuickStatus – close VoiceOver hint"
    },
    "Collapse canvas data" : {
      "comment" : "Canvas – data panel VoiceOver action"
    },
    "Collapsed" : {
      "comment" : "Canvas metric disclosure – VoiceOver value\nCanvas – data panel VoiceOver value"
    },
    "Color Palette" : {

    },
    "Color sources" : {

    },
    "colors" : {
      "comment" : "Category overlay – unit"
    },
    "Colors are not a currency. Well — kind of. You can earn up to 100 per day. Steps and sleep give them to you automatically — 20 each. The other 60 are happenings, and you add those yourself. You can spend colors to unlock apps. But the more you spend, the less colorful your canvas becomes. Because doomscrolling takes color out of life. Literally, here.\n\nI'm not selling them through microtransactions. Colors are yours. You earn them, you deserve them, you can always add more. Within limits." : {
      "comment" : "Note body: about_colors"
    },
    "colors are the currency you earn for living a real life." : {

